+
+**Tests added 2026-11-04 (Critic section 9/10; `tests/decode_reloc_live.sh`, laptop RTX 4060, same tiny model):** (1) `LLAMA_DECODE_RELOC_FAIL=1|2` is a test-only switch that makes the first / the second reserve of the move throw: the run goes on, the experts are put back (log line `expert tensors back in their original (host) buffers`), the log says why, the switch turns itself off, the tokens equal the run with the switch off. (2) A second context created after the move: this found a crash (CUDA illegal memory access): the first context moved back and freed the GPU copy, the second kept a graph reserved while the experts were on the GPU. Fixed with a per-model layout epoch: every move or restore raises it and every context whose scheduler is older drops its graphs before its next batch. (3) Long greedy run, 4 prompts (50 / 700 / 300 / 1500 tokens, the 700 and 1500 arrive in the decode phase and move the layers back), 2400 generated tokens: switch off and on, same ids and same text. **Vulkan at b12064:** a device allocation that fails in the reserve (compute buffer or the patch's own buffer) comes back as a null buffer and `sched_reserve` throws, which the patch catches. The lazy `ggml_vk_preallocate_buffers` at the first compute is different: it rethrows `vk::SystemError`, `llama_decode` has no catch, so a device OOM there ends the process. It only grows buffers that the bigger prompt graph already sized, so it is unlikely but not excluded; the PC test's rule is: the server process must not exit after the line `layers of experts moved`.
+
+**PC run 2026-11-05, nothing moved (fixed):** with the moe-cache plugin the host experts are in the plugin's `MOE_CACHE` buffer, which is not "host" memory, so every layer was skipped, and the log line printed `free 0 MiB` because the memory was never queried. The patch now accepts that buffer (copy through `ggml_backend_tensor_get`, which loads evicted experts first), reads the free memory again for up to 300 ms if it is too low, and its "no layer fits" line gives the real figure or "not queried" plus the skipped layers by reason. `LLAMA_DECODE_RELOC_FAKE_FREE_MIB` (test only) pretends the device has that much free memory. Details: `docs/DECODE_RELOC_DESIGN.md`.
